# Prisma / PostgreSQL Patterns

## Layout
- Schema: `prisma/schema.prisma`
- Client: `src/lib/db/prisma.ts` — reuse the cached `PrismaClient` in serverless
- Mappers: `src/lib/db/catalog.ts`, `orders.ts`, `users.ts`, `serialize.ts`
- Domain queries live in `src/lib/` — never query Prisma from React client components

## Rules
- Use `prisma` from `@/lib/db/prisma` (or `await connectDb()` for call-site compatibility)
- Validate inputs with Zod at the API boundary before writes
- Map rows with `withId` / domain mappers so API responses still expose `_id`
- Use `isDbId()` instead of Mongo ObjectId checks
- Never expose `passwordHash` or secrets in API responses
- Prefer relational includes (`include: { category: true, items: true }`) over N+1 queries
- Nested document-style fields use Prisma `Json` (variants, addresses, attribution, etc.)

## Env (Mentorbridge-style + Prisma password)
```
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=   # used by ensureDatabaseEnv() to derive DATABASE_URL
```
Do not require `DATABASE_URL` / `DIRECT_URL` in `.env` — see `src/lib/db/supabase-database-url.ts`.
